 "turns": [
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you?",
   "est_sec": 2.89,
   "gap_before": 0.41,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_20"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Kind of tired, honestly.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.92,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Me and three flatmates are driving to a wedding in the mountains.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.56,
   "block": "cars.ctx8",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Fun road trip.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.18,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "cars.ctx8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Yeah, but one of them wants the coastal road and the other wants the motorway.",
   "est_sec": 4.75,
   "gap_before": 1.69,
   "block": "cars.ctx8",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Classic. The coastal road is gorgeous but adds about two hours. Do you want scenery, or arriving early with time to change?",
   "est_sec": 6.92,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "cars.ctx8"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Let me think about that for twenty-two seconds, then ask me once more.",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.41,
   "event": "instruction",
   "kind": "think_time",
   "wait_sec": 22,
   "phrasing": "think_instr_29"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Okay, pros and cons.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "anchor": {
    "turn": 6,
    "offset": 12.02
   },
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "self_talk",
   "phrasing": "self_11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "So, the long scenic way, or straight there on the motorway?",
   "est_sec": 3.51,
   "role": "resume",
   "block": "cars.ctx8",
   "anchor": {
    "turn": 6,
    "offset": 22.15
   }
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Oh, also, My father is seventy-nine and he had a fall last month. Are there exercises for balance?",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.87,
   "block": "fitness.dlg21",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Yes, and they really help. Start with simple ones, like standing on one foot while holding a sturdy chair.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 1.03,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "fitness.dlg21"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Holding a chair? He'd hate that.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 1.3,
   "block": "fitness.dlg21",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Safety first, especially after a fall. As he gets steadier, he can hold on with just one finger.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 1.09,
